WEBVTT


00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.899
Witch!


00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:01.199
Forgive me, I have to do this.


00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.999
Witch! Witch!


00:01:07.004 --> 00:01:08.989
Witch! Witch!


00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.976
Witch! Witch!
Witch! Witch!


00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.276
Witch!


00:01:18.101 --> 00:01:21.846
I tried to warn them,
but they wouldn't listen.


00:01:35.106 --> 00:01:37.946
- I tried to save them.
- Witch!


00:02:35.127 --> 00:02:38.180
- Oh shit, thanks, I didn't see that.
- Neither did I.


00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:45.301
People say, "seeing is believing"
But for me that's not entirely true.


00:02:45.302 --> 00:02:49.841
I lost my sight when I was 5 years old.
those memories of what I have seen...


00:02:49.842 --> 00:02:54.171
had faded so much that I doubt
I'd even recognize myself anymore.


00:02:54.172 --> 00:02:58.583
Now I see using my other senses.
I can smell the rain before it drops.


00:02:58.723 --> 00:03:02.615
But I can't watch it fall.
I can feel the sun on my face.


00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:07.024
But I can't see it rise or set.
I want to see the world like everyone else,


00:03:07.025 --> 00:03:10.793
to see the sun, the rain, the music.


00:03:10.794 --> 00:03:13.745
I bet the music looks beautiful.


00:04:07.251 --> 00:04:10.611
Thank you, thank you, thank you.


00:04:10.992 --> 00:04:14.432
It's nice, tastes good.


00:04:15.292 --> 00:04:17.932
- Happy Birthday.
- Thank you.


00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:24.282
- Good evening, Miss Wells.
- Hi, Miguel.


00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:26.633
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:04:27.134 --> 00:04:29.923
- Lilies.
- Came just this morning.


00:04:29.924 --> 00:04:34.154
I sod it up for roses, but uh...
you're the first one that's noticed.


00:04:37.175 --> 00:04:39.254
Nervous about tomorrow?


00:04:39.255 --> 00:04:40.515
No.


00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:47.556
Actually, I have never been
so scared in my entire life.


00:04:47.896 --> 00:04:51.145
Listen, the night before
my mother's surgery,


00:04:51.146 --> 00:04:53.997
she drank two glasses of sherry.


00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:58.757
- Steady as a rock the next day.
- Thank you.


00:04:59.478 --> 00:05:02.118
- Good night.
- Good night.


00:05:16.339 --> 00:05:21.249
This is Dr. Haskins's office calling from County General,
your procedure is still on schedule for tomorrow.


00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:25.821
Be sure to arrive at the hospital 4 hours early
for pre-op. Thank you.


00:05:26.261 --> 00:05:31.100
Hi sweetie, it's your sister,
My flight get's in at 5 am...


00:05:31.101 --> 00:05:35.442
The whole crew's got a layover, so I'll find
someone who'll give me a ride straight to hospital.


00:05:36.582 --> 00:05:40.922
I love you, Sydney,
can't wait to see you. Bye.


00:05:53.344 --> 00:05:55.844
12:10 am.


00:07:20.995 --> 00:07:22.935
- Hello?
- Shhh...


00:07:23.915 --> 00:07:27.484
My (?), she's on from twelve to six
and... well, she takes away my M & M's,


00:07:27.485 --> 00:07:32.156
if I get out of bed.
I'm Alicia, I'm holding out my hand to shake.


00:07:32.236 --> 00:07:34.375
Oh, I'm Sydney.


00:07:34.376 --> 00:07:38.036
I know, Sydney Wells,
I uh... kind a read your chart.


00:07:38.037 --> 00:07:40.137
You had a cornea transfer.


00:07:40.138 --> 00:07:43.037
- How old are you?
- Nine and a half.


00:07:43.097 --> 00:07:47.357
It's just like... well, golf ball
thingies inside my head.


00:07:47.358 --> 00:07:50.107
It makes me sick,
so I can't even ride my bike,


00:07:50.108 --> 00:07:52.147
You see, the doctors
are trying to get it out.


00:07:52.148 --> 00:07:55.608
- When will you get to see?
- Pretty soon, I think.


00:07:55.609 --> 00:07:58.799
Good, I'll come back,
then you... can take a look at me.


00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:03.489
OK. Bye, nice to meet you.


00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.260
Bye.


00:08:12.301 --> 00:08:15.310
I'm starting to lose the
feeling in my fingers.


00:08:15.311 --> 00:08:17.261
Yeah, me too.


00:08:19.362 --> 00:08:21.302
OK...


00:08:21.362 --> 00:08:23.102
- Would you excuse me?
- Yes, Sir.


00:08:23.654 --> 00:08:25.671
Alright.


00:08:27.423 --> 00:08:31.192
- All right, Sydney, now I'll take the bandages off.
- OK.


00:08:31.193 --> 00:08:33.303
- You ready?
- Yeah.


00:08:44.625 --> 00:08:46.545
That's one.


00:08:50.205 --> 00:08:52.025
That's two.


00:08:53.186 --> 00:08:59.426
OK... now, I'm gonna help you...
open your eyes, very slowly.


00:08:59.806 --> 00:09:01.787
- Ok.
- Ok.


00:09:05.247 --> 00:09:07.187
Slowly, slowly, slowly.


00:09:09.228 --> 00:09:11.868
Come on, okay.


00:09:12.728 --> 00:09:15.368
Good... now tell me what you see.


00:09:24.089 --> 00:09:26.110
I can't uh...


00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.470
I'm gonna hold up my hand...


00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:33.791
and I want you to tell me,
how many fingers I have up, ok?


00:09:34.651 --> 00:09:38.431
- Those are fingers?
- Yes, they are.


00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:40.391
Alright, here we go.


00:09:42.162 --> 00:09:45.972
- All of them?
- Yes... very good.


00:09:48.518 --> 00:09:50.039
- Sydney.
- Yeah.


00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:56.633
I want you to try and reach out
and grab my hand... OK.


00:10:03.574 --> 00:10:07.875
It's okay, it’s okay, not everybody
can do this right away, it's okay.


00:10:18.056 --> 00:10:21.005
- It burns a little.
- Is that normal?


00:10:21.006 --> 00:10:23.116
Yeah, it's perfectly normal.


00:10:23.317 --> 00:10:26.237
- Very good.
- Thank you.


00:10:28.817 --> 00:10:31.598
Am I how you pictured it?


00:10:34.018 --> 00:10:35.878
I don't know.


00:10:36.098 --> 00:10:38.838
You're really blurry.


00:10:41.219 --> 00:10:44.808
- I wish mom and dad were here to see this.
- Yeah...


00:10:45.739 --> 00:10:49.480
I think I wanted this more than you, Sydney.


00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.480
Helen, you were twelve...


00:10:54.740 --> 00:11:00.041
I've waited for this for fifteen years.
I thought, I'd feel a sense of uh...


00:11:00.821 --> 00:11:04.962
- It's really freaky...
- It's not your fault... Hey.


00:11:09.382 --> 00:11:11.682
It's not your fault.


00:11:14.663 --> 00:11:16.662
I'm sorry.


00:11:16.663 --> 00:11:19.123
You just need time.


00:11:19.133 --> 00:11:20.843
You'll see.


00:11:26.544 --> 00:11:28.193
Hey, good night.


00:11:28.194 --> 00:11:30.525
- I love you.
- I love you, too.


00:11:46.707 --> 00:11:50.847
Sydney? Can you see me?


00:11:51.327 --> 00:11:53.967
Don't feel bad if you can't.


00:11:54.428 --> 00:11:56.817
What's that on your head?


00:11:56.818 --> 00:11:59.947
A bandana, my grandpa gave it to me.


00:11:59.948 --> 00:12:03.696
You know, maybe tomorrow we can take
a walk and I can show you to park outside.


00:12:03.697 --> 00:12:06.378
- Palm trees and...
- Alicia!


00:12:06.379 --> 00:12:07.218
Oh. coming.


00:12:07.219 --> 00:12:11.330
- Sasquatch, gotta go.
- Bye.


00:12:34.213 --> 00:12:35.893
Please...


00:12:35.913 --> 00:12:38.393
I don't want to go.


00:12:46.954 --> 00:12:48.894
Mrs. Hellman?


00:12:59.755 --> 00:13:01.216
Mrs. Hellman?


00:13:03.855 --> 00:13:05.916
Mrs. Hellman?


00:13:10.877 --> 00:13:13.057
Where're you taking her?


00:13:38.277 --> 00:13:39.657
Oooh...


00:13:44.041 --> 00:13:45.781
Mrs. Hellman?


00:13:46.541 --> 00:13:48.781
Oooohh...


00:14:07.204 --> 00:14:10.744
- Where're you taking her?
- Oh...


00:14:17.204 --> 00:14:19.744
Yeaoohh!


00:14:33.704 --> 00:14:34.944
Oh...


00:14:41.368 --> 00:14:43.288
Freezing.


00:14:45.048 --> 00:14:48.708
Freezing.


00:14:50.409 --> 00:14:54.409
Freezing. Freezing. Freezing.


00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:23.433
Where's Mrs. Hellman?


00:15:24.053 --> 00:15:27.393
Oh, I'm sorry, she passed away last night.


00:15:35.414 --> 00:15:38.804
Everything looks just perfect.


00:15:38.805 --> 00:15:43.075
You're recovering quite nicely,
and the tearing has stopped?


00:15:43.335 --> 00:15:46.716
- I think so... yeah.
- Good.


00:15:50.036 --> 00:15:54.206
- Uhm... so, who's eyes were these?
- Excuse me?


00:15:54.207 --> 00:15:55.946
My uh... my donor?


00:15:55.947 --> 00:15:59.306
I'm afraid I can't help you with that, Sydney.
There’re your eyes now and they're working.


00:15:59.307 --> 00:16:02.497
I shouldn't matter where they came from.
That hurt?


00:16:02.498 --> 00:16:04.798
Yeah, a little.


00:16:08.658 --> 00:16:11.599
When will I be able to see more clearly?


00:16:11.819 --> 00:16:15.488
Well, it varies with each patient.
A couple of days, a couple weeks.


00:16:15.489 --> 00:16:20.009
But your vision itself isn't the issue,
since you've been blind so long.


00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:24.320
I'm going to refer you to a specialist.
Paul Faulkner, he helps you.


00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.561
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:16:28.661 --> 00:16:33.321
- Alright, have a nice day off tomorrow.
- Thanks, Sydney. - OK.


00:17:52.991 --> 00:17:53.951
Hi.


00:17:54.391 --> 00:17:55.651
Hey.


00:17:57.231 --> 00:17:59.532
Are you ready to be my tour guide?


00:17:59.992 --> 00:18:01.271
You're leaving?


00:18:01.272 --> 00:18:04.250
Yeah, I'm afraid they had enough of me here.


00:18:04.251 --> 00:18:07.352
- This is my sister Helen, Helen, this is Alicia.
- Hi.


00:18:07.353 --> 00:18:10.222
- Hey, can we get a picture together?
- Of course.


00:18:10.223 --> 00:18:12.373
- I'll do it.
- Okay.


00:18:18.794 --> 00:18:22.734
I know you're scared, Sydney.
Don't be.


00:18:22.915 --> 00:18:26.575
The world it's... it's really beautiful.


00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:29.175
Ok... smile.


00:18:32.956 --> 00:18:38.075
My (?) is in the trunk, I just could
put it on your couch, you know, I could...


00:18:38.076 --> 00:18:40.137
bring your meals, clean, and get
us in some art galleries.


00:18:40.997 --> 00:18:45.316
Is it too much for you? I mean, you want me
to pull over or something? Just say the word.


00:18:45.317 --> 00:18:49.147
No, no, no we can talk every day, you can
come over and check on me, I just...


00:18:49.948 --> 00:18:53.197
I really think, I just need to do
something on my own, okay?


00:18:53.198 --> 00:18:55.358
Okay, I understand.


00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:07.940
- I got some new lambs for your place.
- Oh, thanks.


00:19:07.941 --> 00:19:09.125
Just take a minute.


00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.980
- Here, I'll do it.
- Okay.


00:19:18.761 --> 00:19:20.581
Surprise.


00:19:25.682 --> 00:19:29.882
- It's too soon, I know, I don't know what I was thinking.
- It's okay.


00:19:30.883 --> 00:19:33.852
- Well, do I know any of you?
- Welcome home.


00:19:33.853 --> 00:19:36.672
Oh, hi Jim.
How are you?


00:19:36.673 --> 00:19:38.873
- Nice to see you.
- Nice to see you, too.


00:19:38.874 --> 00:19:41.904
Sydney, it's Brett.
Welcome home.


00:19:42.205 --> 00:19:45.723
- Hey, Sid, it's me, Alex from the upstairs.
- Hi.


00:19:45.724 --> 00:19:50.385
- God, nice to see you.
- It's your cousin, Sarah.


00:19:50.425 --> 00:19:54.795
- Oh, Sarah... it's been so long.
- I'm so happy.


00:19:54.796 --> 00:19:59.336
- Recognize my voice?
- Hi, Cynthia.


00:19:59.346 --> 00:20:01.966
- You knew it was me.
- How could I not, Cynthia.


00:20:01.967 --> 00:20:02.966
Hello, girl.


00:20:03.407 --> 00:20:07.107
- Oh, Richard, hi.
- How you're doing?


00:20:08.967 --> 00:20:12.247
- So, this is what bald looks like.
- Mm'hm.


00:20:12.248 --> 00:20:16.567
- Hey, Sydney. How are you?
- Miguel, how are you?


00:20:16.568 --> 00:20:18.808
- You look good.
- Oh, honey thanks.


00:20:19.249 --> 00:20:24.308
- Hello honey, how're you feeling?
- This is all so...


00:20:24.809 --> 00:20:26.749
Take a breath.


00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.560
Are you okay?
Do you need some water or anything?


00:20:37.561 --> 00:20:40.631
Yeah, I'm gonna go to the kitchen.
Why don't you stay with the guest.


00:20:40.641 --> 00:20:44.512
That's OK.
Oh, thank you guys for coming.


00:22:38.225 --> 00:22:40.886
1:06 am.


00:22:56.648 --> 00:22:58.047
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:22:58.048 --> 00:22:59.568
Sorry, I'm late.


00:23:00.128 --> 00:23:01.648
That's Henry.


00:23:04.509 --> 00:23:07.049
- I'm Paul.
- Sydney.


00:23:10.429 --> 00:23:12.009
Have a seat.


00:23:25.071 --> 00:23:27.500
You damaged your cornea
when you were five?


00:23:27.501 --> 00:23:30.201
Yeah, my sister and I were
playing with firecrackers.


00:23:30.202 --> 00:23:34.152
I tried a transplant, when I was 12.
But I rejected them.


00:23:34.172 --> 00:23:39.013
Uhm, 10/76, refused it then.
Have you tried again?


00:23:39.113 --> 00:23:43.753
No, my sister was really the one
who kept up with all that stuff.


00:23:49.794 --> 00:23:55.624
These are Dr. Haskin's test results, there's nothing
physically wrong with you, the operation went...


00:23:55.625 --> 00:23:59.147
- flawlessly, but you're probably in for a shock.
- Why?


00:23:59.148 --> 00:24:02.345
You've already felt the information
from sound, smell and touch.


00:24:02.346 --> 00:24:08.536
But now, you're gonna be assaulting a million
things you never even knew existed.


00:24:09.276 --> 00:24:11.996
It's a whole new level of confusion.


00:24:11.997 --> 00:24:15.626
Gonna look here, see there... is that
bright thing important,


00:24:15.627 --> 00:24:18.316
or this dark one, moving
toward me or away from me...


00:24:18.317 --> 00:24:20.127
dangerous or not?


00:24:20.128 --> 00:24:24.557
As long as your eyes are open,
there's just too many distractions,


00:24:24.558 --> 00:24:27.939
I mean, how do you concentrate?
I'm talking to you and...


00:24:28.199 --> 00:24:32.539
you're looking at that woman and
you're thinking, is she gonna eat that?


00:24:32.639 --> 00:24:35.209
That's a pineapple, by the way, cut it open.


00:24:35.210 --> 00:24:37.820
I like pineapple.


00:24:38.600 --> 00:24:40.069
Sorry.


00:24:40.070 --> 00:24:44.080
Anyway, because you can see, people gonna
expect you to do things, that you can't do.


00:24:44.081 --> 00:24:47.950
Read signs, recognize body language, people's
gestures and facial expressions...


00:24:47.951 --> 00:24:51.621
you just get out of their way,
your eyes will wanna dominate...


00:24:51.622 --> 00:24:55.221
how you perceive the world,
but you can't fully trust them, not yet.


00:24:55.222 --> 00:24:59.021
In the next few weeks, I'm gonna help
you to see the world like it really is, okay?


00:24:59.022 --> 00:25:04.332
Some of it's gonna be wonderful, a lot of it's gonna
be difficult, but the main thing is, to be prepared.


00:25:04.333 --> 00:25:08.864
And that's where I come in.
We're in this together.


00:26:39.014 --> 00:26:41.195
You scared me.


00:26:54.256 --> 00:26:57.717
Have you seen my report card?


00:26:57.897 --> 00:27:00.037
Your report card?


00:27:02.417 --> 00:27:06.558
- Do you live here, sweetie?
- My father will be so mad at me.


00:27:07.218 --> 00:27:10.038
Have you seen my report card?


00:27:51.023 --> 00:27:52.763
Sorry.


00:27:52.943 --> 00:27:54.604
Let's take five.


00:27:55.144 --> 00:27:58.444
I'm sorry, I don't know what's
wrong with me.


00:27:59.064 --> 00:28:00.724
Relax.


00:28:00.904 --> 00:28:03.085
You're pushing too hard.


00:28:15.506 --> 00:28:18.956
You know, when I first went to London
to work with the Philharmonic...


00:28:18.957 --> 00:28:25.207
I was so nervous, in Prague, I was a
big fish, in London, there were hundreds.


00:28:26.347 --> 00:28:28.808
But you did very well in London.


00:28:29.188 --> 00:28:34.958
I never thought I would be ready,
but when it was time to go on...


00:28:34.959 --> 00:28:39.209
everything faded away,
it was just me.


00:28:42.269 --> 00:28:45.130
Then there was nothing to worry about.


00:28:45.669 --> 00:28:46.930
You know...


00:28:49.991 --> 00:28:52.691
Sydney.


00:28:52.991 --> 00:28:56.691
Will you be ready?
We're all counting on you.


00:28:58.151 --> 00:29:01.452
- I'll be ready.
- I'm sure you'll be.


00:29:01.672 --> 00:29:04.772
- 22.
- 22? That's us.


00:29:06.032 --> 00:29:08.052
- You sit tide, I'll get it.
- Thank you.


00:29:08.092 --> 00:29:09.852
- 22?
- Yea.


00:29:19.274 --> 00:29:22.494
You think I'm just gonna let you go?


00:29:23.314 --> 00:29:26.695
- You think, I'm not gonna do something?
- That's right!


00:29:30.635 --> 00:29:33.745
- I'm gonna do it.
- I'm sorry.


00:29:33.746 --> 00:29:36.416
I told you I was gonna do it.


00:29:40.446 --> 00:29:41.916
That's all I got.


00:29:58.839 --> 00:30:01.059
What's happened?


00:30:01.719 --> 00:30:07.540
- There was a woman, she came at me.
- What woman?


00:30:08.160 --> 00:30:10.020
What woman?


00:30:11.020 --> 00:30:14.620
Christ, Sydney, get
a hold off yourself, please.


00:30:15.761 --> 00:30:17.541
Sorry.


00:30:17.681 --> 00:30:19.421
Sorry.


00:30:21.241 --> 00:30:23.822
- I apologize.
- It's all right.


00:31:00.297 --> 00:31:04.237
Witch! Witch! Witch!


00:32:22.297 --> 00:32:25.237
- The ordinary scope from the spec analysis
- And that's good, right?


00:32:27.297 --> 00:32:29.437
Well.


00:32:30.597 --> 00:32:35.438
From the latest results, there's
nothing wrong with your eyes.


00:32:37.678 --> 00:32:40.477
Well, maybe there's something
wrong with the tests.


00:32:40.478 --> 00:32:43.218
The tests only gave us the fact,
that you gave them up normal responses.


00:32:43.219 --> 00:32:47.088
Creative ones yes, like the kind
that artists and musicians give.


00:32:47.089 --> 00:32:49.399
But last I checked, you are a musician.


00:32:49.479 --> 00:32:54.060
I'm sure other musicians don't
see what I've been seeing.


00:32:54.080 --> 00:32:55.560
Come with me.


00:32:55.561 --> 00:32:57.749
I'm not an idiot.


00:32:57.750 --> 00:33:01.510
I understand what you're telling me, my
brain's having to re-learn how to decode...


00:33:01.511 --> 00:33:06.021
the world around it, but that's very different
for me seeing things, that don't seem to be real.


00:33:06.022 --> 00:33:10.262
- How?
- Look, you're real, OK.


00:33:11.762 --> 00:33:13.902
You're here.


00:33:14.282 --> 00:33:18.232
My perspective and focus is off, but...


00:33:18.233 --> 00:33:22.183
you're real, I can see you.


00:33:27.444 --> 00:33:32.264
We see what we look at, but the way that
we see things, is the fact by what we know,


00:33:32.265 --> 00:33:34.564
and there's a lot around you, that
can't make any sense to you.


00:33:34.565 --> 00:33:36.385
What are you saying to me?


00:33:37.205 --> 00:33:43.285
You think I'm making this up?
You think I want this to be happening to me?


00:33:43.286 --> 00:33:46.795
You think you might not be able to push through this,
you think you were better before.


00:33:46.796 --> 00:33:53.107
More special... well, you just discovered
that now you're like the rest of us.


